+FILLED (B7, 2026-10-22; HOL proof architecture `k = 4,3,2,1,0`). The omega
+chain agrees by `p2e_NJIUTIU` throughout, so `HD ul = HD vl` comes straight from
+its `i = 0` instance (no `ROGERS_INTER_V_LEMMA` needed). `k = 4`:
+nonemptiness gives `hl ul < sqrt 2`; `p2e_TEZFFSK` at `k = 3` identifies the full
+lists. `k = 3,2,1`: nonemptiness gives the circumradius regime
+(`hl (truncateSimplex (k-1) ul) < sqrt 2`, `sqrt 2 ≤ hl ul`); `p2e_TEZFFSK` at
+`k - 1` identifies the truncation, `p2e_p13_dd_hl_ge_of_omega_eq` transfers
+`sqrt 2 ≤ hl vl`, and `mxi` agrees by `p2e_p13_dd_mxi_eq_of_omega` (which uses
+`p2e_p13_dd_hl_trunc2_ge_of_omega_eq`, `p2e_WAUFCHE1/2`, `p2e_OMEGA_LIST_LEMMA`,
+`p2e_HD_TRUNCATE_SIMPLEX`). `k = 2` additionally reads `{u0,u1} = {v0,v1}` off
+the shared truncation (`p2e_BARV_3_EXPLICIT` + `p2e_TRUNCATE_SIMPLEX_EXPLICIT_1`),
+`k = 1`'s tail case discharges the `rconeGt` factor by
+`p2e_RCONE_GT_EQ_EMPTY_LEMMA` once `sqrt 2 ≤ hl (truncateSimplex 1 ·)`, and
+`k = 0` is the shared Rogers simplex minus the same ball. Cell definitions
+dispatch via `p2e_MCELL_EXPLICIT`. -/
